And he was called Parson because he'd been a Methodist horse preacher, which meant that he basically just sort of trudged around on a horse. He wasn't preaching to horses. No, preaching to revivalist meetings. Francis Fassisi. Exactly. Parson Brownlow is a very abrasive, stubborn, vituperative man. Everybody agrees.
