them voting and they helped redeem the South from the horrors of reconstruction. But historians now generally say the idea that the freedmen were taken in by these sort of tricks is itself a racist myth. As Alan Trellis says, this is actually a story not about black superstition about ghosts. it's a story about white superstitions about black people because it basically the white, the clansmen are playing these tricks and laughing and saying to them each other
